---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ContactSection from "../components/ContactSection.astro";
import FaqItem from "../components/FaqItem.astro";
import ServiceAreaSection from "../components/ServiceAreaSection.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import plus440 from "../assets/machines/plus-440-angle.jpg";
import max620 from "../assets/machines/max-620-angle.jpg";
import ultra1200 from "../assets/machines/ultra-1200-angle.jpg";
import freezer550 from "../assets/machines/freezer-550-front.jpg";

const title = "Smart Cooler & Smart Market Services | Crossbell Vending";
const description =
  "Compare Crossbell smart cooler vending and secure smart market service for workplaces and shared spaces across Macomb and north Oakland County, Michigan.";

const areaServed = site.serviceArea
  .flatMap((entry) => entry.name.split("/").map((city) => city.trim()))
  .map((city) => ({ "@type": "City", name: `${city}, MI` }));

const serviceSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "@id": `${site.url}/services/#managed-smart-vending`,
  name: "Managed smart vending service",
  serviceType: "Smart cooler vending and secure smart market installation, stocking, and service",
  description,
  url: `${site.url}/services/`,
  provider: { "@id": `${site.url}/#organization` },
  areaServed,
  hasOfferCatalog: {
    "@type": "OfferCatalog",
    name: "Smart vending formats",
    itemListElement: [
      {
        "@type": "Offer",
        itemOffered: {
          "@type": "Service",
          name: "Smart cooler vending",
          description: "A single secure, cashless smart cooler installed, stocked, and serviced by Crossbell Vending.",
        },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Offer",
        itemOffered: {
          "@type": "Service",
          name: "Smart market service",
          description: "A coordinated group of secure smart coolers and freezers managed as one onsite market.",
        },
      },
    ],
  },
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} contactHref="#contact" schema={serviceSchema}>
  <!-- Hero: the measured bay is a real equipment decision, not decoration. -->
  <section class="overflow-hidden bg-indigo text-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1280px] lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
      <div class="flex flex-col justify-center px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:py-24 lg:pr-14 lg:pl-[max(2rem,calc((100vw-1120px)/2+2rem))]">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent uppercase">
          Smart vending, sized to the room
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-[15.5ch] text-[clamp(2.7rem,5vw,4.25rem)] font-bold leading-[0.98] text-white">
          One cooler when that's enough. A complete smart market when it isn't.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[52ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-lavender">
          Crossbell builds the setup around your traffic, floor space, and the food people ask for.
          We install it, stock it, monitor it, and keep it running on our Macomb and north Oakland route.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3.5">
          <a
            href="#contact"
            class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-[3px] bg-accent px-6 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hover"
          >
            Request a site visit
          </a>
          <a
            href="#compare"
            class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-[3px] border-2 border-lavender px-6 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-white hover:text-indigo"
          >
            Compare the formats
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-lavender">No-cost equipment and service for qualifying locations.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative border-t border-indigo-2 bg-white px-5 pt-10 pb-7 text-ink sm:px-10 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l">
        <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 bg-accent px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-bold tracking-[0.16em] text-ink uppercase">
          Placement study · 02 doors
        </div>
        <div class="flex min-h-[360px] items-end justify-center pt-7 sm:min-h-[500px]">
          <Image
            src={ultra1200}
            alt="Two-door smart cooler shown at a three-quarter angle"
            widths={[520, 760, 1000]}
            sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 46vw, 90vw"
            class="h-auto max-h-[480px] w-full object-contain"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="sync"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="relative mt-2 border-t-2 border-ink pt-4">
          <span class="absolute -top-2 left-0 h-4 border-l-2 border-ink"></span>
          <span class="absolute -top-2 right-0 h-4 border-r-2 border-ink"></span>
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-6 font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] uppercase">
            <span>53.9 in cabinet width</span>
            <span class="text-right text-accent-dim">Tap · take · close</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-accent text-ink" aria-label="Service commitments">
    <dl class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1120px] divide-y divide-ink/20 px-5 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:divide-x sm:divide-y-0 sm:px-8">
      <div class="py-6 sm:pr-8">
        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase">One local operator</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">The people who answer also run the route.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6 sm:px-8">
        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase">Remote + weekly</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">Inventory is watched between scheduled visits.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6 sm:pl-8">
        <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase">Right-sized first</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">We recommend the smallest setup that serves the site well.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- Two formats, presented as a decision rather than a generic feature grid. -->
  <section id="compare" class="scroll-mt-20 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="format-heading">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-5 sm:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-[60ch]">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Choose by use, not by model</p>
        <h2 id="format-heading" class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] font-semibold">
          Start with the room. Then choose the hardware.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[1.04rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Both formats use the same secure, cashless checkout and the same Crossbell service route.
          The difference is how much selection the location can support.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 border-y-2 border-ink">
        <article id="smart-cooler" class="grid scroll-mt-24 gap-5 border-b border-line py-7 md:grid-cols-[90px_1fr_240px] md:items-start md:gap-8">
          <div class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-accent-dim">FORMAT 01</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[clamp(1.65rem,3vw,2.2rem)] font-semibold">Smart cooler vending</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-[58ch] text-muted">
              One secure glass-door cooler with automatic checkout. It gives a smaller break room,
              gym, lobby, or waiting area a useful mix without taking over the wall.
            </p>
            <a href="#cooler-detail" class="mt-4 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4">
              See the single-station setup ↓
            </a>
          </div>
          <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 border-l-0 border-line md:grid-cols-1 md:border-l md:pl-6">
            <div><dt class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-muted uppercase">Doors</dt><dd class="mt-1 font-semibold">One or two</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-muted uppercase">Best fit</dt><dd class="mt-1 font-semibold">Compact spaces</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article id="smart-market" class="grid scroll-mt-24 gap-5 py-7 md:grid-cols-[90px_1fr_240px] md:items-start md:gap-8">
          <div class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-accent-dim">FORMAT 02</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[clamp(1.65rem,3vw,2.2rem)] font-semibold">Smart market</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-[58ch] text-muted">
              A coordinated group of coolers and freezers managed as one onsite store. It adds
              room for more drinks, snacks, fresh choices, frozen items, and site-specific essentials.
            </p>
            <a href="#market-detail" class="mt-4 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4">
              See how the market grows ↓
            </a>
          </div>
          <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 border-l-0 border-line md:grid-cols-1 md:border-l md:pl-6">
            <div><dt class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-muted uppercase">Doors</dt><dd class="mt-1 font-semibold">Two or more</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-muted uppercase">Best fit</dt><dd class="mt-1 font-semibold">Busy, multi-shift sites</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cooler-detail" class="scroll-mt-20 bg-lavender-tint py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1120px] gap-10 px-5 sm:px-8 md:grid-cols-[0.82fr_1.18fr] md:items-center">
      <figure class="border border-line bg-white p-5 sm:p-8">
        <Image
          src={plus440}
          alt="Single-door smart cooler shown at a three-quarter angle"
          widths={[460, 720, 900]}
          sizes="(min-width: 768px) 38vw, 90vw"
          class="mx-auto h-auto max-h-[520px] w-full object-contain"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-4 border-t border-line pt-3 font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-muted uppercase">
          Single station · 26.8 in example footprint
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Smart cooler vending</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] font-semibold">A small store behind one door.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[56ch] text-[1.04rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Customers tap a card or phone to unlock, take one item or several, and close the door.
          The cooler records what left and completes the purchase automatically—no product coils,
          no barcode scanning, and no separate kiosk.
        </p>
        <dl class="mt-7 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-5 border-t border-line pt-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Selection</dt><dd class="mt-1">Cold drinks, snacks, protein, fresh options, and premium items.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Checkout</dt><dd class="mt-1">Credit or debit card, Apple Pay, and Google Pay.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Site needs</dt><dd class="mt-1">A level indoor spot, service access, and one standard outlet.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Service</dt><dd class="mt-1">Weekly route visits with remote inventory checks in between.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a href="/machines/" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-[3px] bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hover">
            Compare cooler sizes
          </a>
          <a href="/contact/?service=smart-cooler" class="text-sm font-semibold underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4">
            Ask about a cooler
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="market-detail" class="scroll-mt-20 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-5 sm:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.72fr_1.28fr] lg:items-end">
        <div class="pb-1">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Smart market</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] font-semibold">Build the market one bay at a time.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-[50ch] text-[1.04rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
            A smart market is not one oversized machine. It is a deliberate mix of refrigerated
            and frozen capacity, matched to the room and serviced as one Crossbell location.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-[50ch] text-muted">
            Start with the traffic and the product mix. Add doors only when the site needs them.
            That keeps the footprint useful instead of filling a wall for appearance's sake.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Signature service-bay diagram using approved, model-specific product imagery. -->
        <figure class="border-2 border-ink bg-white">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-4 py-3">
            <span class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase">Example service bay</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-semibold text-accent-dim uppercase">Configured after walkthrough</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[0.78fr_1.42fr_0.8fr] divide-x divide-line">
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col px-2 pt-4 sm:px-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-muted uppercase">Cooler</span>
              <Image src={max620} alt="Single-door smart cooler module" widths={[260, 420]} sizes="20vw" class="mt-auto h-auto w-full object-contain" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col px-2 pt-4 sm:px-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-muted uppercase">Double-door cooler</span>
              <Image src={ultra1200} alt="Double-door smart cooler module" widths={[380, 620]} sizes="32vw" class="mt-auto h-auto w-full object-contain" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col px-2 pt-4 sm:px-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] text-muted uppercase">Freezer</span>
              <Image src={freezer550} alt="Single-door smart freezer module" widths={[260, 420]} sizes="20vw" class="mt-auto h-auto w-full object-contain" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="border-t-2 border-ink px-4 py-3 text-sm text-muted">
            An example, not a fixed package. The final mix depends on space, traffic, shifts, and what people will buy.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="bg-paper p-5"><div class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Drinks</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Water, soda, energy, sports drinks, juice, and cold brew.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-paper p-5"><div class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Snacks</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Everyday favorites, protein, better-for-you choices, and local requests.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-paper p-5"><div class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Fresh + frozen</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Ready-to-eat options and frozen items where the location supports them.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-paper p-5"><div class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Site essentials</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Personal care, convenience, or premium items chosen for the audience.</p></div>
      </div>

      <aside class="mt-8 grid gap-4 border-l-4 border-accent bg-lavender-tint p-5 sm:p-7 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] md:gap-8">
        <h3 class="font-body text-base font-semibold">Why “smart market”?</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          A traditional micro market puts products on open shelves and checks customers out at a
          central kiosk. Crossbell's smart market keeps products inside secure coolers and freezers;
          checkout happens at each door. It delivers broad selection without an open retail floor.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div class="mt-8">
        <a href="/contact/?service=smart-market" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-[3px] bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hover">
          Ask about a smart market
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-indigo py-14 text-paper sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="checkout-heading">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-5 sm:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-[56ch]">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent uppercase">The customer side</p>
        <h2 id="checkout-heading" class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] font-semibold text-white">Four actions. No kiosk lesson.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="mt-10 grid border-y border-indigo-2 sm:grid-cols-4 sm:divide-x sm:divide-indigo-2">
        <li class="border-b border-indigo-2 py-6 sm:border-b-0 sm:px-5 sm:first:pl-0">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-accent">01 / TAP</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-lavender">Tap a card or mobile wallet at the reader.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="border-b border-indigo-2 py-6 sm:border-b-0 sm:px-5">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-accent">02 / OPEN</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-lavender">The door unlocks after payment authorization.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="border-b border-indigo-2 py-6 sm:border-b-0 sm:px-5">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-accent">03 / TAKE</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-lavender">Choose one item or several in the same visit.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="py-6 sm:pr-0 sm:pl-5">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-accent">04 / CLOSE</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-lavender">The system records the items and completes checkout.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="responsibility-heading">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-5 sm:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-[58ch]">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Clear responsibilities</p>
        <h2 id="responsibility-heading" class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] font-semibold">You provide the place. We run the market.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-9 grid border-2 border-ink md:grid-cols-2 md:divide-x md:divide-ink">
        <div class="p-6 sm:p-8">
          <h3 class="font-body text-lg font-semibold">Crossbell handles</h3>
          <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 text-muted sm:grid-cols-2">
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Equipment and delivery</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Installation and setup</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Product selection</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Stocking and rotation</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Remote inventory checks</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Cleaning, service, and repairs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t-2 border-ink bg-lavender-tint p-6 sm:p-8 md:border-t-0">
          <h3 class="font-body text-lg font-semibold">Your location provides</h3>
          <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 text-muted sm:grid-cols-2">
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">A suitable indoor space</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Standard wall power</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Access for route service</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3">Enough daily use to support the setup</li>
            <li class="border-t border-line pt-3 sm:col-span-2">Honest feedback about what people want stocked</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceAreaSection />

  <section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-20 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[880px] px-5 sm:px-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-dim uppercase">Service FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] font-semibold">Before we measure the room</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 border-t border-line">
        <FaqItem question="What is the difference between a smart cooler and a smart market?">
          A smart cooler is one self-contained, cashless station. A smart market combines two or more
          coolers or freezers to carry a broader mix at a busier location. Crossbell manages the full
          setup as one stop on our route.
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Is this the same as an open-shelf micro market?">
          No. An open-shelf micro market uses fixtures and a central self-checkout kiosk. A Crossbell
          smart market keeps products behind controlled doors and handles checkout at each cabinet.
          That makes it a better fit where open shelves or a separate kiosk are not practical.
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Does the host pay for the equipment or service?">
          Qualifying locations pay no equipment, delivery, stocking, or service charge. We confirm fit
          during the walkthrough because a larger smart market needs enough regular traffic to stay
          fresh and useful.
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="How much space and power do we need?">
          A single cooler starts at 22.8 inches wide. Larger coolers and multi-unit markets need more
          wall space, and each cabinet needs access to standard power. We measure the actual placement,
          door swing, walking clearance, and outlet access before recommending anything.
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Who decides what gets stocked?">
          We start with the site type, shift pattern, and expected traffic, then adjust from real sales
          and requests. The point is not to force the same planogram into every location—it is to stock
          the mix your people will actually use.
        </FaqItem>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSection
    id="contact"
    heading="Request a smart vending walkthrough"
    subheading="Tell us about the room, the people who use it, and when they are there. We'll recommend a single cooler or a smart market after a ten-minute site visit."
  />
</Layout>
